@CC =========================================  

@CC = LOADING XMSG INTER  SYSTEM VERSION    =

@CC =========================================  


@MODE (UTILITY)XMSG-LOAD-L:MODE,,

@CC

@CC   ****************************************************************

@CC   **  Load or reload XMSG version L for XPIT - SINTRAN III/VSX. **

@CC   ****************************************************************

@CC   *

@CC   * PREREQUISITES - IMPORTANT - PREREQUISITES - IMPORTANT:

@CC   *    a) Sintran III VSX

@CC   *    b) Sintran III version K (or later)

@CC   *

@CC   * 1) The product (BPUN) files must have been installed properly.

@CC   *    If not, read the Product Description Sheet supplied with

@CC   *    the XMSG floppy disks and install XMSG.

@CC   * 2) Unless the XMSG files was copied to user UTILITY, edit this

@CC   *    file accordingly:

@CC   *    Substitute (UTILITY)

@CC   *    with       (Name of user which has the XMSG :BPUN files).

@CC

@CC   

@CC   * Now you can (re)load XMSG to:

@CC   *   1.  Load XMSG-KERNEL onto its segment.

@CC   *   2.  Load XMSG-XROUT onto its segment.

@CC   *   3.  Load XMSG-FIDO onto its segment.

@CC   *   4.  Create the foreground programs XROUT,

@CC   *       XTRACE and XMFIDO.

@CC 

@HOLD 0 0

@HOLD 3 2

@SINTRAN

*@STOP-XMSG

ERROR: XMSG has not been loaded
*@EXIT

@HOLD 0 0

@HOLD 3 2

@UNFIX 33

@RT-LOADER


REAL TIME LOADER,  SINTRAN III VSX - K

*READ-BINARY (UTILITY)XMSG-KERNEL-L:BPUN,33,,,

CHANGING EXISTING SEGMENT? YES
*END
*READ-BINARY (UTILITY)XMSG-XROUT-L:BPUN,34,,

CHANGING EXISTING SEGMENT? YES
*END
*CLEAR-SEG SXMFIDO

SEGMENT NAME NOT DEFINED
*Y
*NEW-SEG SXMFIDO,,,,,,
NEW SEGMENT NO:    72
*READ-PROG (UTILITY)XMSG-FIDO-L:PROG,SXMFIDO,,
*END
*DECLARE-PROGRAM XROUT,,,
*CHAN-RT-DESC XROUT,100,34,33,0,,2,2,
*DECLARE-PROGRAM XTRACE,,,,
*CHAN-RT-DESC XTRACE,100,34,33,2,,2,2,
*DECLARE-PROGRAM XMFIDO,,,
*CHANG-RT-DESC XMFIDO,36,SXMFIDO,,0,,,,,
*END
*WRITE-SEG S3XMSGP,,,,,,


  SEG.  SEG.    LOWER  UPPER  MASS  SEG. RING PIT SEG.  SEG.
  NO.   NAME    ADDR.  ADDR.  ADDR. FILE          PROT  TYPE

    33 S3XMSGP 120000 177777  1656    0    2   2  RFW   NON DEMAND PROTECT
*WRITE-SEG S3XMSGD,,,,,,


  SEG.  SEG.    LOWER  UPPER  MASS  SEG. RING PIT SEG.  SEG.
  NO.   NAME    ADDR.  ADDR.  ADDR. FILE          PROT  TYPE

    34 S3XMSGD      0 117777  1706    0    2   2  RFW   DEMAND PROTECT
*WRITE-SEG SXMFIDO,,,,,,


  SEG.  SEG.    LOWER  UPPER  MASS  SEG. RING PIT SEG.  SEG.
  NO.   NAME    ADDR.  ADDR.  ADDR. FILE          PROT  TYPE

    72 SXMFIDO      0 115777  7536    0    0   1  RFW   NON DEMAND
*EXIT

@CC

@CC   * 4.  Patch in DPIT and IMAGE to flag XMSG loaded (XMSGU+4)

@CC

@LOO-AT SEG S3DPIT
READY:
4170/ 000000 -1
 000000 .
-END

@LOO-AT SEG S3IDPIT
READY:
4170/ 000000 -1
 000000 .
-END

@CC  

@CC  And now you can start XMSG by using the SINTRAN-SERVICE command START-XMSG.

@CC


